      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, a winding curl of stairs led deep into the dark. At the very top step sat Mosk, an old grey fox wearing a patched green vest. His voice sounded like dry leaves skittering on stone as he warned Lina that the tree was not for visitors and she should return home to forget the humming. Lina stood tall, insisting she could not possibly forget a melody she had not yet heard."
